--   Test Description
--
--   This test ensures that the GEM can operate properly up to the maximum number of collisions (15) in 10 or 100 mode.
--
--   Functional Coverage
--   * Ensures that the GEM operates properly when up to 15 collisions occur in 10 or 100 mode. (The GEM should retry transmission of a frame for up to a maximum of 15 times after back-off.)
--   * Ensures that the GEM flags a collision frame statistic when more than 15 collisions occur in 10 or 100 mode. 
--   * Also toggles crs to get to INTERFRAME_GAP_BOFF state in transmit state machine.
--
--   Detailed Test Description
--
--   1. Initialise GEM for 10M mode operation.
--   2. Enable all interrupts
--   3. Reduce back off time to one slot-time by writing bit 12 of the 
--      config register
--   4. write tx buffer q pointer
--   5. write tx_go
--   6. Transmit a frame and at the beginning of the data portion of the 
--      frame cause a collision.
--   7. The GEM back-offs and one slot time later re-tries to retransmit 
--      the frame.
--   8. Repeat steps 6 and 7 fourteen more times.
--   9. After the 15th collision the frame should be transmitted properly 
--      after the back-off period.
--  10. Have a second frame queued up for transmission and check this is 
--      successfully transmitted
--  11. Check status and statistics registers and ensure that the above 
--      operations were handled properly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------



-- ************************************************************************** --
--   1. Initialise GEM for 100M mode operation.
--   2. Enable all interrupts
--   3. Reduce back off time to one slot-time by writing bit 12 of the 
--      config register
--   4. write tx buffer q pointer
--   5. write tx_go
-- ************************************************************************** --
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      04 00081000  -- reduce backoff time to one slot time
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd     138 00000000  -- check single collisions frames
apbrd     13C 00000000  -- check multiple collisions frames
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit
apbrd      14 00000000  -- read transmit status register
apbwr      1c ffffff00  -- write address of transmit buffer descriptor
apbrd      1c ffffff00  -- check transmit queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000208  -- write transmit start bit and enable tx


-- ************************************************************************** --
--   6. Transmit a frame and at the beginning of the data portion of the 
--      frame cause a collision.
--   7. The GEM back-offs and one slot time later re-tries to retransmit 
